The first adversary run caught a real construction leak: XORing the displayed diagonal recovered the determinant on every odd-order instance (the sampled eight happened to record it as 3/8 only because zero/format edge cases obscured some successes). I’m replacing the permutation skeleton by a determinant-one, all-ones-preserving rank-one perturbation. This keeps the paper’s compact invariant route but destroys the trace shortcut; I’ll rerun every gate afterward.
