-{"paper": "1804.11172", "difficulty": "hard", "params": {"n": 20, "seed": 2080967113}, "question": "Determinant orbit of a fat subspace over GF(2^128)\n\nWork in the finite field F = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1). A field element is\nwritten as exactly 32 hexadecimal digits: bit e is the coefficient of x^e,\nfor 0 <= e <= 127. Addition is bitwise XOR. Multiplication is ordinary\npolynomial multiplication over GF(2), reduced by x^128=x^7+x^2+x+1.\n\nThe 41 rows of the matrix A below are an ordered GF(2)-basis of a\nGF(2)-subspace U of F^41. They are promised to be linearly independent\nover F, so U is a fat 41-subspace in the terminology of the paper.\nFor q=2, the determinant orbit invariant of U is simply det_F(A), because\nGF(2)^*={1}. Compute that nonzero field element exactly.\n\nMatrix A (41 rows and 41 columns; spaces separate entries):\n70bc10c6088c918ff52ff1a39fee27ed 707a5a664a2828a37d64f2690b491aad e20758ac8433d24212458f6db41d373f 5f0faaff21db30acc94d9a6fd02e6247 12531c44ec115d205c54dde7c8603e91 a93cd490d34f21548de52b32c9a0e9aa 780e775e223c03a1213c6b8adf061d88 2ba71d530fd517659fe8cc111c4fef1c 12531c44ec115d205c54dde7c8603e91 1dac96b1294e25e57fa8491bfd068004 97466980a7eb043a1589e3c0b3c20557 0bbfe32bd7001c4e2d996f649fdc6883 923a6662b159e8b70e9b5349f8401b7e 0bbfe32bd7001c4e2d996f649fdc6883 f35c5ef227f9f740595aa9d3be77c139 923a6662b159e8b70e9b5349f8401b7e 2ba71d530fd517659fe8cc111c4fef1c 97466980a7eb043a1589e3c0b3c20557 0adc1885f4c93e852884146b9f826158 b7f2c5dabac97d60a607797a197500fd b7f2c5dabac97d60a607797a197500fd d11d3501c3389cdd9b6b914df80e30e5 0d7b2a5cfeac19d5a667b045f9f093e9 229c1bae1432e759b570e4d780d0324d be5028f33ced2d5f9a19e877045ea084 05864d0a722fa53b1a6389a839ff7c62 05864d0a722fa53b1a6389a839ff7c62 70bc10c6088c918ff52ff1a39fee27ed 80a92a0291ae33c1c91293aa23a3e695 229c1bae1432e759b570e4d780d0324d d11d3501c3389cdd9b6b914df80e30e4 f35c5ef227f9f740595aa9d3be77c139 be5028f33ced2d5f9a19e877045ea084 780e775e223c03a1213c6b8adf061d88 a93cd490d34f21548de52b