-{"paper": "1804.11172", "difficulty": "hard", "params": {"n": 20, "seed": 1478781934}, "question": "Determinant orbit of a fat subspace over GF(2^128)\n\nWork in the finite field F = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1). A field element is\nwritten as exactly 32 hexadecimal digits: bit e is the coefficient of x^e,\nfor 0 <= e <= 127. Addition is bitwise XOR. Multiplication is ordinary\npolynomial multiplication over GF(2), reduced by x^128=x^7+x^2+x+1.\n\nThe 41 rows of the matrix A below are an ordered GF(2)-basis of a\nGF(2)-subspace U of F^41. They are promised to be linearly independent\nover F, so U is a fat 41-subspace in the terminology of the paper.\nFor q=2, the determinant orbit invariant of U is simply det_F(A), because\nGF(2)^*={1}. Compute that nonzero field element exactly.\n\nMatrix A (41 rows and 41 columns; spaces separate entries):\n0cf35b9e8d2a700886d3823aefb55e08 0a3e4d731255f741fe1db88e9aaf6233 ba1e24042cd231e88635f5a6b895d4f6 adfc21c753769a72386b3bda8c32ce58 cc0f2f3f1b17e6af852334b0ec143b30 ba1e24042cd231e88635f5a6b895d4f6 6066132960c6e9b86f71306c4bf79dd9 5f9fbba9298f464c8709dbd85da35103 0cf35b9e8d2a700886d3823aefb55e08 9367da38287c891247d09437c430e502 f09e97c0b2b00eb61f7f48475a990c2f 90d2f1f0734de8384dd5b5127060d105 cfdcba58aeb93a1ec6dd2ac7ae64b54c 0a3e4d731255f741fe1db88e9aaf6233 57a311eff15fcc36dc0603db8ac94b5c 57a311eff15fcc36dc0603db8ac94b5c 90d2f1f0734de8384dd5b5127060d105 f09e97c0b2b00eb61f7f48475a990c2f 7699005bc6ce83fec0237cd0d1cf9b09 fab07db1f44ab1025818d589bf1658bd fab07db1f44ab1025818d589bf1658bd 9faa45b23cf35556c6fe7b37a48a70ad 2745aa051ce5bb933c74ff95442635ae 861fe06b87cc82aa251b35c26b393a2c e6d8ea363f5267b935a879642dc8d3d5 a8ad27e55141451862323c3e3f13f57d 5bd343b1f818d9446b1dd246aa51770f 861fe06b87cc82aa251b35c26b393a2c ccb55d081676515f0c22c298740b2b84 7699005bc6ce83fec0237cd0d1cf9b09 cc0f2f3f1b17e6af852334b0ec143b30 cfdcba58aeb93a1ec6dd2ac7ae64b54c adfc21c753769a72386b3bda8c32ce59 5f9fbba9298f464c8709dbd85da35103 5bd343b1f818d9446b1dd2