-{"paper": "1804.11172", "difficulty": "hard", "params": {"n": 20, "seed": 60353406}, "question": "Determinant orbit of a fat subspace over GF(2^128)\n\nWork in the finite field F = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1). A field element is\nwritten as exactly 32 hexadecimal digits: bit e is the coefficient of x^e,\nfor 0 <= e <= 127. Addition is bitwise XOR. Multiplication is ordinary\npolynomial multiplication over GF(2), reduced by x^128=x^7+x^2+x+1.\n\nThe 41 rows of the matrix A below are an ordered GF(2)-basis of a\nGF(2)-subspace U of F^41. They are promised to be linearly independent\nover F, so U is a fat 41-subspace in the terminology of the paper.\nFor q=2, the determinant orbit invariant of U is simply det_F(A), because\nGF(2)^*={1}. Compute that nonzero field element exactly.\n\nMatrix A (41 rows and 41 columns; spaces separate entries):\n4175039cd69b11d2d7b5e12fa2873081 680ecdd4fb75a98203a20d40aac0b4ff 72ab9009335bea77e7536a0f5d22b0ae ac77301f58eb1f5f4f56a37940bb1311 740274a3704d436841117b9ab5b1aa8a 671d75bb2c1395d8a78f88f72d358a01 ac77301f58eb1f5f4f56a37940bb1311 82c239b69fc86f5dc3d88c68fdb82c6f 82c239b69fc86f5dc3d88c68fdb82c6f f4a35310641044854283ff53b1f4681a 30192ce5d6eca70758a7106f09f382f8 d89e588f5eb966391b2b05dff13772f1 46a3b0d98d86819ae946b60ff265671f 740274a3704d436841117b9ab5b1aa8a 57d890be534a8461473af0bb8e80423d 572c91e8d931188022eadbdc11199451 29de0bb58c3dbbbf39d3d387f0e7cd12 72ab9009335bea77e7536a0f5d22b0ae 4175039cd69b11d2d7b5e12fa2873081 f4a35310641044854283ff53b1f4681a 14a10354de00be4dca40456adf22185a 30192ce5d6eca70758a7106f09f382f8 671d75bb2c1395d8a78f88f72d358a01 69e8efcd6b20e9aac403aa6c2ceb0d2a 69e8efcd6b20e9aac403aa6c2ceb0d2a 60c06e3f67394fc00f665af0e3731a8a 14a10354de00be4dca40456adf22185a 54db33545c8b3b2b745bc7aee856cda0 184d6b2872eca5d9c98e28ada5c37a09 9e5310d3985af6ffe79eac10963063b8 1d638f06bd12783ce28ae2950a7b0b79 184d6b2872eca5d9c98e28ada5c37a09 d89e588f5eb966391b2b05dff13772f0 46a3b0d98d86819ae946b60ff265671f 54db33545c8b3b2b745bc7ae