-{"paper": "1804.11172", "difficulty": "hard", "params": {"n": 20, "seed": 1325996281}, "question": "Determinant orbit of a fat subspace over GF(2^128)\n\nWork in the finite field F = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1). A field element is\nwritten as exactly 32 hexadecimal digits: bit e is the coefficient of x^e,\nfor 0 <= e <= 127. Addition is bitwise XOR. Multiplication is ordinary\npolynomial multiplication over GF(2), reduced by x^128=x^7+x^2+x+1.\n\nThe 41 rows of the matrix A below are an ordered GF(2)-basis of a\nGF(2)-subspace U of F^41. They are promised to be linearly independent\nover F, so U is a fat 41-subspace in the terminology of the paper.\nFor q=2, the determinant orbit invariant of U is simply det_F(A), because\nGF(2)^*={1}. Compute that nonzero field element exactly.\n\nMatrix A (41 rows and 41 columns; spaces separate entries):\n1ede7c73e679bd720496be906d6b765f 53f92868b784c5a93e1cdf9b8aaa672e 2bc8cc15e76fa0b24ca8b5a72d83fc3d 00ff22fdfdadab825c347104982e8b24 250a885c21117194eab4a29f23fff613 8d439de977cacbf6ef11f77174e2e351 250a885c21117194eab4a29f23fff613 dc7318b46d238f19aafcff5837bc1878 1e0fbabf7f906e100f3d15e999544543 688609caca7dd7c7859d20b1e6aad8a5 1ede7c73e679bd720496be906d6b765f 8d4e5f9446995a747daa51497d7e739f dbf1cee232aa7dd0fea54bf8b8bc0e58 1d2d89678c4521cff0c99742c074542b 129b9d29c29a879356fa003e56d5fd2f 08b98c20d4505351ffbe077e0070e840 5d50016fd9fee6fa9d87167d1236ec26 dbf1cee232aa7dd0fea54bf8b8bc0e58 32b0162be098e484e7a4922afebae17c 688609caca7dd7c7859d20b1e6aad8a5 9a9e109fc174cdf2c458bba89b68de52 8e87675852210e4ab5932b2a19ee3a15 129b9d29c29a879356fa003e56d5fd2f 1e0fbabf7f906e100f3d15e999544542 08b98c20d4505351ffbe077e0070e840 32b0162be098e484e7a4922afebae17c 5d50016fd9fee6fa9d87167d1236ec26 00ff22fdfdadab825c347104982e8b24 8d4e5f9446995a747daa51497d7e739f 0d1c33188f60db88d783ba75cfc4aa24 94221d30d13cb1b62c5b476978b1071b 1d2d89678c4521cff0c99742c074542b 8e87675852210e4ab5932b2a19ee3a15 9a9e109fc174cdf2c458bba89b68de52 53f92868b784c5a93e1cdf