-{"paper": "1804.11172", "difficulty": "hard", "params": {"n": 20, "seed": 963138955}, "question": "Determinant orbit of a fat subspace over GF(2^128)\n\nWork in the finite field F = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1). A field element is\nwritten as exactly 32 hexadecimal digits: bit e is the coefficient of x^e,\nfor 0 <= e <= 127. Addition is bitwise XOR. Multiplication is ordinary\npolynomial multiplication over GF(2), reduced by x^128=x^7+x^2+x+1.\n\nThe 41 rows of the matrix A below are an ordered GF(2)-basis of a\nGF(2)-subspace U of F^41. They are promised to be linearly independent\nover F, so U is a fat 41-subspace in the terminology of the paper.\nFor q=2, the determinant orbit invariant of U is simply det_F(A), because\nGF(2)^*={1}. Compute that nonzero field element exactly.\n\nMatrix A (41 rows and 41 columns; spaces separate entries):\n9152fb126d6549eff30fd48bb4dc089b 9152fb126d6549eff30fd48bb4dc089b 6f9c49a2ef91a7eab9fb1ef4b60ad09d 7d4ebfb02e2b92d81196bc7d2bc91073 b89d04634a0e8cd589197495532ab012 b89d04634a0e8cd589197495532ab012 20c7922c003e91ad3abef960b8bf9e87 aed77d23116aa9fdbc78700eab4199a3 b0005893658cc6cf5bf73db2233f5b05 daf95318412b5b54b60f801ac3d1b605 c01953c4841190036ced36e7c3122026 20c7922c003e91ad3abef960b8bf9e87 b0005893658cc6cf5bf73db2233f5b05 384f85b1581158ef97b89c392688ff1a 26d9b4017979f8f4824796c8ccc100e8 34e1e58dea44a89a91921433f7672176 56dc3048790aa92e8b0796f14a60d332 384f85b1581158ef97b89c392688ff1a 7d4ebfb02e2b92d81196bc7d2bc91072 7d7bf1bc49ae9091a6256b907108de0e fddc1ed9864c34ed00743fd446cefcf2 ee39722e92337e1ce0a245bb1d7f9cd0 a9fd2240cd95e961c8dcc6edc73c15cd 6c22f5b3fc9f7c59bf2408023dc18efc 1b032b65a55a5a9e7331ad0e0197eeee 8f809b321634ba91f1e94b412a418f82 34e1e58dea44a89a91921433f7672176 1b032b65a55a5a9e7331ad0e0197eeee ee39722e92337e1ce0a245bb1d7f9cd0 a9fd2240cd95e961c8dcc6edc73c15cd 6c22f5b3fc9f7c59bf2408023dc18efc de04b55f7754a118a2917cf5655ad9f2 de04b55f7754a118a2917cf5655ad9f2 7d7bf1bc49ae9091a6256b907108de0e aed77d23116aa9fdbc78700