-{"paper": "1804.11172", "difficulty": "hard", "params": {"n": 20, "seed": 865105336}, "question": "Determinant orbit of a fat subspace over GF(2^128)\n\nWork in the finite field F = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1). A field element is\nwritten as exactly 32 hexadecimal digits: bit e is the coefficient of x^e,\nfor 0 <= e <= 127. Addition is bitwise XOR. Multiplication is ordinary\npolynomial multiplication over GF(2), reduced by x^128=x^7+x^2+x+1.\n\nThe 41 rows of the matrix A below are an ordered GF(2)-basis of a\nGF(2)-subspace U of F^41. They are promised to be linearly independent\nover F, so U is a fat 41-subspace in the terminology of the paper.\nFor q=2, the determinant orbit invariant of U is simply det_F(A), because\nGF(2)^*={1}. Compute that nonzero field element exactly.\n\nMatrix A (41 rows and 41 columns; spaces separate entries):\na3d4f332c707a9ec2ccf689bac1fc2e2 6efd12f78e617b0e4be736b67bb2d779 673246a81e90c6ef4fdba1ab9e74098d 2ad010b5a6a82d3ceb77e082e8e9d182 d78bbe9f44267a4595a9dc4e9bc7217a ccd8764b1f829d62af74f5ce40b6f8d6 08dc8cb217f389eab6d982b7df058b40 f9dfec631963cf340bc81a0461f19621 2ac93f2f59ef0282f9af1d9736a4ae28 c41455b7b5b57a007112044017b1c0a4 16ad08664350711f89e1859f2b903955 08dc8cb217f389eab6d982b7df058b40 ccd8764b1f829d62af74f5ce40b6f8d6 597ae077a236ea3c306b39ef0c7ab0f9 476dcd859818d482a2fd897297bcaa0c d78bbe9f44267a4595a9dc4e9bc7217a 2e4c7ffd52d3de3c2ab1f89853a3e9b6 2e72f0aeef1eaa3298de615302a29e6b 3ad8418093a38e5a3fd034bc748ef324 7a06cb2722ad97727d1ca13531d78a76 336e7208d7296077a3ec43cc7e816708 476dcd859818d482a2fd897297bcaa0c c41455b7b5b57a007112044017b1c0a4 16ad08664350711f89e1859f2b903955 2ad010b5a6a82d3ceb77e082e8e9d182 a3d4f332c707a9ec2ccf689bac1fc2e2 597ae077a236ea3c306b39ef0c7ab0f9 3ad8418093a38e5a3fd034bc748ef324 2e4c7ffd52d3de3c2ab1f89853a3e9b6 f25e5534876101481cd37ef94c33af7c f25e5534876101481cd37ef94c33af7c cd8a2a6e54732edf47698a680957ff82 336e7208d7296077a3ec43cc7e816709 2e72f0aeef1eaa3298de615302a29e6b cd8a2a6e54732edf47698a6