codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator grounded in Lemma 8 and Theorem 4 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1804.11172v2#S5).

Files:

- [gen_1804_11172.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.11172/gen_1804_11172.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.11172/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.11172/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.11172/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.11172/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1804.11172/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local G1–G9 gates pass:

- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability `1/(2^128−1)`.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Gaussian reference algorithm: 8/8, as expected for Track B.
- Shipping answer: 245 characters, 77 elements, approximately 62 tokens.
- Intended route: 41 field additions.
- Canonical-key tests: 20/20 invariant and 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.

The required oracle evaluation remains externally blocked: every bare, hinted, and placebo call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before inference. Consequently, no Step 4 hardness verdict is claimed, and the README marks the family as not submission-ready. I retained the error transcripts and did not create `REJECTED.md`.

A validation attempt briefly produced an unvalidated artifact and “done” claim; I removed both. They are regenerable after a successful hardening run.
